  "text": "Home Products Pricing Blog Help Sign in Five tomato varieties for small balconies By Sam Ortiz · April 3 Growing tomatoes in containers is easier than most people think. The key is choosing compact, determinate varieties that fruit early and do not need tall stakes. 1. Tumbling Tom A trailing cherry tomato that works well in hanging baskets. 2. Balconi Red Bred for window boxes, it rarely grows taller than 40 cm. 3. Tiny Tim An heirloom dwarf that fruits in about 55 days. Share Read comments (14) Privacy Terms Contact us © 2026 Example Inc.",
